  "notes": "Australian Agricultural Company (AACo) — ASX-listed integrated cattle producer. Fiscal year ends 31 March; H1 ends 30 September. Owns ~6.4M ha (~15.8M acres) of cattle stations across Northern Territory and Queensland, plus feedlots and Darwin abattoir (mothballed 2018). IFRS reporting with biological assets (cattle herd) carried at fair value, and pastoral land/property carried at fair value through directors' valuations supplemented by independent appraisals (LAWD). Statutory results highly volatile due to non-cash livestock and property revaluations; AACo discloses operating EBITDA pre-revaluation as primary KPI. Brand-led wagyu/branded beef strategy (Westholme, Darling Downs, 1824). Production reported in kg meat sold and head-of-cattle. Pre-2010 history: AACo relisted on ASX August 2001 via the AA Trust restructure with ~7.0M ha; portfolio peaked at ~7.7M ha (2007-09 incl. Brunette Downs, Wrotham Park, Headingly, Avon Downs etc.). FY02-FY09 results from published Annual Reports; herd reported in head, station portfolio in million hectares.",
